-- 0064: Edappadi DTCP plot schedule + traced plan geometry.
--
-- Jamin Garden — Edappadi had plots_total NULL and an empty plot_layout, so the
-- Master plan tab could only show the static drawing. This fills in the real
-- schedule from the sanctioned approval drawing (DTCP application
-- LP/EDP/2026/0148, 27 plots, blocks A-J with no block "I") and adds the traced
-- plan geometry so the tab can draw an interactive, tappable plan.
--
-- plot_layout keeps the shape this app already uses — {plot, size_sqft, facing,
-- status} — so the existing availability legend and the pipe-delimited plot
-- schedule editors keep working untouched. The extra keys (block, size_sqm,
-- dim_m, poly, at, clipped) are what the interactive plan draws.
--
-- Geometry is traced from the approval PDF's vector content stream, so the plan
-- is verifiable against the legal sheet rather than redrawn by eye. `poly` is
-- the outline as the sheet actually draws it: eight plots run past the site
-- boundary and the drawing clips them to it. Sizes and areas come from the plot
-- schedule on sheet 2, never from the coordinates.

alter table public.properties add column if not exists plot_plan jsonb;

comment on column public.properties.plot_plan is
  'Traced site-plan geometry for the interactive plot map: viewBox, boundary, '
  'OSR, roads, dimension callouts, metresPerUnit and the area statement. '
  'Display only — quoted sizes and areas come from plot_layout.';

update public.properties
